<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Estonian War of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a>–<a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Estonian War of Independence was fought by the new Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> against Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and then the Baltic German Landeswehr. With British naval support and Finnish volunteers, Estonian forces drove out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> in early 1919 and defeated the Landeswehr at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesis">Cēsis</a> in June. The Treaty of Tartu in February 1920 secured Estonian independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/estonian-war-of-independence.jpg" alt="Estonian War of Independence" width="320" height="273" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mmh; derivative work by Reimgild · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Estonian_War_of_Independence,_map.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
